WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.767
-Welcome to the show.
They love you.

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:04.968
-Thank you so much.
Everyone's so lovely.

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:06.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Aww. It's a good crowd.

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:08.868
-Wow. Hi.

00:00:08.868 --> 00:00:12.701
-I was asking you earlier if you
ever met Keanu Reeves before.

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:16.033
-Ah. The wonderful --
One time I have met him.

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:18.901
I was at an event,
and he was also there.

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:21.434
And we were kind of
the two introverts

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:23.601
on the outskirts of the party.

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:25.701
And we were just kind of
sitting there, like --

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:27.734
And then he said,
"Do you have a pet?"

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:29.601
And I said,
"I do. I have a dog."

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:31.434
And he went,
"Do you have any pictures

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:33.067
of your dog in costume?"

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:34.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.968
-Interesting question.
-It was so sweet.

00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:39.767
And I said, "I sure do."
-You actually had a photo...

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:41.334
-Oh, yes.
-...of your dog in a costume?

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:42.634
-Yeah.

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:44.234
-And you brought that photo
for us. Look at this.

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:46.534
-Yeah.
[ Audience awws ]

00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:48.868
-[ Laughs ] Oh, come on.
Mouse.

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:51.801
-That's my sweet Mouse,
who's no longer with us.

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:54.267
-No longer with us.
Mouse, we love you, pal.

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:56.100
Making a debut
on "The Tonight Show."

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.934
-I know.

00:00:57.934 --> 00:00:59.501
-Do you enjoy coming
to New York City?

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:01.634
Oh, I love it.
I love it so much.

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:04.300
-Do you have -- What are your
memories of this great city?

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.767
-The first time I ever came
here, I think I was 16,

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:10.567
and I was doing a press tour
for "Heavenly Creatures."

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:12.767
And Kate Winslet and I
were staying

00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:15.601
at the Four Seasons,
and Kate said,

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.868
"Oh, the minibar. You can take
everything out of it.

00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:19.834
And they just put it in
the next day."

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:22.167
And I was like, "Oh, my gosh."

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:25.501
So every day we were
clearing out the minibar

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:27.968
and just filling up
our suitcases

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:29.734
and being like,
"More stuff comes."

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:32.133
-Oh, my God!
-And we were just lying

00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:34.534
on the bed just watching,
like, the first ten minutes

00:01:34.534 --> 00:01:38.400
of every movie just like,
"No, not that one."

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.734
And then we got a call
from Miramax,

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:42.367
from the company
distributing the film,

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:46.300
saying, "This is
the worst room-service bill."

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.801
-"You guys got to slow down."
-Yeah. They were like,

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:51.000
"What's going on in there?"

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.801
We're like, "Oh, gosh. Sorry."
Like, just clearing the minibar.

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:55.767
-First getting a minibar,
you're just like,

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:57.834
"What is this?
This is the most insane thing."

00:01:57.834 --> 00:01:59.100
-I know. I couldn't believe It.
It was like magic.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.234
-Yeah, it is magic.

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:01.467
I was like,
"They just bring more?"

00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:02.501
She was like, "Yes."

00:02:02.501 --> 00:02:03.834
-My first time
staying at a hotel,

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:05.934
I remember, like, freaking out
of how many rolls

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:07.601
of toilet paper they had, too.

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:10.067
I'm like, "Spare rolls of
toilet -- This is unbelievable!"

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:11.601
-I know.
-Like, I just freaked out.

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:14.734
Yeah. A minibar. You're like,
"This is -- I'm in paradise."

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:18.167
After that, is that when you
worked with Drew Barrymore?

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:20.534
-Yes. Yeah. My next movie
was with Drew Barrymore.

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:22.968
-"Ever After."
-Angel. Yes. Yes.

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:24.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:24.501 --> 00:02:27.200
-How great is -- I know we --
everyone loves Drew Barrymore,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.467
but, really, don't you just love
Drew Barrymore?

00:02:29.467 --> 00:02:31.334
-Oh, she's just, like,
the most special,

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:32.868
the kindest person.

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:34.267
I had this moment.

00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:36.367
She gave me a gift when
we started doing "Ever After."

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:37.567
And it was so sweet.

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:39.501
And I was like,
"I want to get her a gift."

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:41.634
And I found,
at this antique market,

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:45.067
these plates with a butterfly
opening in different stages.

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:47.000
I was like, "Perfect."

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.834
And I gave them to her,
and she was like,

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:50.501
[as Barrymore] "Oh, my God!

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:54.300
If each one of these plates
was to fall to the floor

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:58.834
and smash into
a thousand million pieces,

00:02:58.834 --> 00:03:00.934
each one of the pieces
would scream,

00:03:00.934 --> 00:03:02.501
'I love you, Melanie.'"

00:03:02.501 --> 00:03:05.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.234 --> 00:03:06.567
Like --

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:08.400
-Oh, my gosh.
-In the moment.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:12.200
-That is unbelievable!

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.200
-I'm so nervous.
I'm so nervous.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:15.534
It wasn't a very good
impression,

00:03:15.534 --> 00:03:16.834
but just the moment...

00:03:16.834 --> 00:03:18.200
-Unbelievable impression.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:21.267
That is exactly Drew,
by the way. That is her.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.434
-But, like, in the moment
of receiving the gift,

00:03:23.434 --> 00:03:25.167
that's what came
out of her mouth.

00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:27.167
It was the most beautiful,
poetic, like...

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:29.267
I just was like,
"Oh, you're a fairy.

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:30.734
You're like a living..."

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:31.934
-She really is a fairy.
She's a living --

00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:33.267
Yeah, she's unbelievable.
-Amazing person.

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:35.734
-Before we get into
"Yellowjackets,"

00:03:35.734 --> 00:03:38.100
which frightens me, scares me --
-I'm sorry.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:41.133
-Yeah. It's the most frightening
thing I've ever seen in my life.

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:42.734
-Yeah.
-It's a brilliant story.

00:03:42.734 --> 00:03:44.067
But I want to get to that.

00:03:44.067 --> 00:03:46.667
But also, speaking of scary,
"The Last of Us."

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:48.701
You were fantastic.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:48.701 --> 00:03:50.501
"The Last of Us."
-Thank you.

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:52.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:53.300
-You're great.
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.400
She's a horrible person.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.467
-Yeah, it's interesting how
you're playing these roles.

00:03:57.467 --> 00:03:59.033
You're such a nice person,
but, yeah.

00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:01.868
-Something needs to come out,
apparently.

00:04:01.868 --> 00:04:03.267
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:04.534
Your husband, Jason Ritter,

00:04:04.534 --> 00:04:06.801
who is very talented
and funny and nice.

00:04:06.801 --> 00:04:10.000
He is actually --
You said he's in episode --

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.434
or one of the episodes
of "Last of Us."

00:04:11.434 --> 00:04:14.100
-He's in episode five, yeah.
-And I go -- I didn't see him.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.467
I don't remember.
Because I love him.

00:04:15.467 --> 00:04:17.801
I'm a fan. And I go,
"I don't remember him."

00:04:17.801 --> 00:04:19.801
And you go, "Yeah.
He was one of the..."

00:04:19.801 --> 00:04:21.801
-He was a stunt person.

00:04:21.801 --> 00:04:23.801
He trained
with the stunt people,

00:04:23.801 --> 00:04:26.267
and he just did
all these amazing stunts.

00:04:26.267 --> 00:04:27.934
It's, like, his lifelong dream.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:30.400
He got put in the makeup,
and he came out of the ground

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.400
and was falling over
and doing all these --

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:33.834
I shot him once.

00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:35.033
-You shot him once?
-Yeah.

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:37.167
-Why not? Yeah. Of course.
-Why not?

00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:39.534
-Here's a picture
of you two backstage

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:41.200
in "The Last of Us" there.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.133
[ Audience awws ]

00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:44.734
He looks great.

00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:46.534
[ Laughs ]

00:04:46.534 --> 00:04:48.267
-So romantic.
-It's so romantic.

00:04:48.267 --> 00:04:50.000
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.033
-I want to talk
about "Yellowjackets."

00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:53.901
Because here we go.
This is season two.

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:58.601
And, honestly, I thought the
premise was just so brilliant.

00:04:58.601 --> 00:05:01.434
I'm still guessing. I still
don't know what's going on.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:03.534
[ Laughter ]
Really.

00:05:03.534 --> 00:05:06.467
-I don't either, by the way.
You know?

00:05:06.467 --> 00:05:11.300
-How do we describe the show,
just the basic story line?

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:13.801
-Well, the basic story line,
there's a plane crash

00:05:13.801 --> 00:05:15.567
in the '90s in the wilderness.

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:19.334
A group of teenage female
soccer players are stranded.

00:05:19.334 --> 00:05:22.334
They're forced to do
terrible things to survive.

00:05:22.334 --> 00:05:24.100
And then the other half
of the story

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:26.667
takes place in the present day
with --

00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:29.801
It follows four,
now this season, six

00:05:29.801 --> 00:05:31.634
of the survivors
of the plane crash.

00:05:31.634 --> 00:05:33.300
-And no one really knows

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.167
what happened
when they were stranded.

00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:36.667
-Yeah.
-And that story starts

00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:38.801
to come out, and it is bonkers.

00:05:38.801 --> 00:05:41.834
-It is bonkers. Yeah.
-It is so unbelievable.

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:44.267
Everyone's great in it,
but, gosh, you were so good.

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:48.634
And season two --
-There were moments, like --

00:05:48.634 --> 00:05:51.667
I would get a script and read
what they were having someone do

00:05:51.667 --> 00:05:53.634
and just text, like,
Sophie Nélisse,

00:05:53.634 --> 00:05:54.834
who plays little me.

00:05:54.834 --> 00:05:56.901
I was like,
"Are you going to be okay?

00:05:56.901 --> 00:05:58.934
-Oh, my God.
-Will you be okay?"

00:05:58.934 --> 00:06:00.667
She was like,
"I think I can do it."

00:06:00.667 --> 00:06:02.601
She's so talented.
She's so amazing.

00:06:02.601 --> 00:06:04.567
I mean, I love all of them.
-It's well done.

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:06.267
Everybody is so great.

00:06:06.267 --> 00:06:08.534
It is a must-watch
if you haven't seen it.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:11.167
Congrats on all the awards
that you've received for this

00:06:11.167 --> 00:06:12.300
and been nominated for it.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:14.167
Well, well, well deserved.
-Thank you.

00:06:14.167 --> 00:06:16.167
-I want to show a clip.

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:19.167
Here's Melanie Lynskey in
season two of "Yellowjackets."

00:06:19.167 --> 00:06:20.467
Take a look.

00:06:20.467 --> 00:06:23.400
-Miss Sadecki,
do you understand your rights

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.634
as I have explained them to you?

00:06:25.634 --> 00:06:27.868
-Yes, I -- I do.

00:06:27.868 --> 00:06:30.601
-Why did you kill Adam Martin?

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:35.901
-What? I -- I didn't.
-Didn't what?

00:06:35.901 --> 00:06:40.734
-I didn't murder
Adam -- whoever.

00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:43.834
I -- I didn't murder anyone.

00:06:43.834 --> 00:06:45.834
-I never said he was murdered.

00:06:45.834 --> 00:06:48.834
-But -- But you said
someone killed him.

00:06:48.834 --> 00:06:50.801
-So how was the sex?

00:06:50.801 --> 00:06:54.868
Mind-blowing or just, like,
really, really hot?

00:06:54.868 --> 00:06:57.367
-They're definitely
not going to ask me that.

00:06:57.367 --> 00:06:59.901
-Oh. So he couldn't
get it up, huh?

00:06:59.901 --> 00:07:02.234
Is that why you murdered him?
-Okay.

00:07:02.234 --> 00:07:03.934
So I think we're done here.

00:07:03.934 --> 00:07:07.701
-Yeah, I think we're done here.
Melanie Lynskey, everybody.

00:07:07.701 --> 00:07:09.868
Season two of "Yellowjackets"

00:07:09.868 --> 00:07:12.501
premieres March 24th
on Showtime.

00:07:12.501 --> 00:07:15.968
We're talking De La Soul
after the break. Come on back.

